WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
- [Narrator] Think of Party
City like this balloon

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.170
from one of its stores.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.340
When it IPOed in 2015,
the company was floating.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.070
Now not so much.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.140
Shares are down 99%

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:16.170
and the company has filed for bankruptcy.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:19.020
Party City's downfall was
caused by a unique set

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.200
of circumstances, changing
consumer behaviors,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:26.130
inflation, and ballooning helium prices.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:28.173
So what went wrong?

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.170
Party City opened the doors
to its first store in 1989,

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.270
but the Party City shoppers know today

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.270
really started to take shape in 2005

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.880
when it was bought by
two private equity firms.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:44.730
And then years later by another firm.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:46.530
- They added businesses to them,

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:49.830
they acquired other suppliers,

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:53.550
and they also expanded the
store footprint tremendously.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.850
- [Narrator] Under new owners,
Party City's party grew.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:59.910
Revenue increased and debt decreased.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:02.910
Plus, it gained about 90 stores.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:06.150
In 2015, Party City went public again.

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:10.230
- These private equity firms
were also acquiring businesses

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:11.700
and adding to the company

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.130
and also growing the store footprint.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.130
So all of that made it more
attractive as a public company.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.210
- [Narrator] While Party
City share price fell

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.740
after the IPO, it stayed
steady until about 2019.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.990
On an earnings call in May of that year,

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:32.370
Party City announced about 5%
of its stores were closing.

00:01:32.370 --> 00:01:35.190
- [Jim] We have decided to
close approximately 45 stores

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.050
over the course of 2019.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:41.130
- [Narrator] One Driving
factor, declining balloon sales.

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.060
Metallic balloon sales
had fallen 8.4% due to...

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:47.100
- A global helium shortage.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:50.040
- The helium shortage, they
say it's getting too expensive

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.720
to fill up all those balloons.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.640
- Helium's pretty important for Party City

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:58.640
because a lot of the
traction of the retail chain

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:02.910
for customers is the
balloons that you can get.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.700
- [Narrator] The US'
helium shortage wasn't new.

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.460
It became a problem in the late 2000s,

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:13.440
but by 2019, it was
deflating Party City sales.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.420
Helium is sourced as a byproduct

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.490
from natural gas extraction,

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:19.890
but a lack of new natural
gas infrastructure

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:23.130
coming online in the US hurt supply.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:25.590
That drove up prices of the noble gas,

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.710
and Party City's stock fell.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:30.900
Then in the fall of 2019,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.900
the company was dealt an even bigger blow.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.190
- [Jim] Overall, the Halloween season

00:02:35.190 --> 00:02:36.540
was below expectations.

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.100
- [Narrator] Revenue in October,

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.020
a key month for the company

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.260
declined 7% from the year before

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.010
and sales at its Halloween
only stores, Halloween City,

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:49.260
dropped about 20%.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.990
- Party City faced a lot of competition,

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.990
for example, from Spirit Halloween.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:56.940
And then of course, in the last 20 years,

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.360
consumers have been shifting
more to online shopping,

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:01.980
so that's also hurt them.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:02.880
- [Narrator] In recent years,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.580
the company has faced many
of the same challenges

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:09.060
affecting other retailers
like changing consumer habits

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:11.313
due to the pandemic and inflation.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.520
The pandemic led to smaller gatherings

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.160
and less demand for Party City's products.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:20.220
- Even even though the
pandemic is coming to an end,

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.640
what the executives at
Party City have said is that

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.930
they're still finding,

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:26.910
that people are still
having smaller gatherings

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:28.260
than they used to.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.730
- [Narrator] So as a result,

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.963
sales and the company's stock
price have continued to fall.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:38.520
Then last December, Party City
hired restructuring advisors

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.333
to evaluate how best to
handle its lack of cash.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.660
On January 6th, people
familiar with the matter

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:49.113
said the retailer was planning
to file for bankruptcy.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:54.950
Party City shares dropped
57% to just 15 cents.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.390
- It definitely indicates
that investors think

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:01.200
that you're probably gonna
at least file for bankruptcy

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:04.200
and maybe not survive at all as a company.

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.730
- [Narrator] On January 18th,

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:08.970
the company officially
filed for bankruptcy.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:13.800
Party City said, it plans to
reduce its 1.4 billion in debt

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.890
and exit bankruptcy within four months.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.100
The company is also evaluating
its store footprint,

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:23.340
including identifying
underperforming stores.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:25.590
It's already closed 28.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:28.020
Party City declined to comment further.

00:04:28.020 --> 00:04:30.480
- Party City, when they
come out of bankruptcy,

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.550
if things go according to plan

00:04:32.550 --> 00:04:34.440
should shed a lot of their debt.

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.350
And what that means is
that interest that they pay

00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.150
will be a lot lower

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:42.900
and lowered than it has been for years.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.550
- [Narrator] Party City's future success

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.860
will depend on whether
the company can emerge

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:51.303
from bankruptcy and develop a
strategy to restart the party.

